### Liveness
GET http://localhost:3000/live

### Readiness (503 while shutting down or a dependency is down)
GET http://localhost:3000/ready

### Slow request holding a DB connection (max 5000 ms)
GET http://localhost:3000/work?ms=500

### Marketplace: a company (also creates its wallet). Duplicate e-mail, any case -> 409
# @name seller
POST http://localhost:3000/companies
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "ООО Продавец", "email": "seller@example.com" }

###
# @name buyer
POST http://localhost:3000/companies
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "ООО Покупатель", "email": "buyer@example.com" }

### Administrator credits the wallet by a bank notification. Same notification again -> 409
POST http://localhost:3000/companies/{{buyer.response.body.id}}/wallet/deposits
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bankNotificationId": "BN-2026-0001", "amount": 30000000 }

### Seller publishes a lot (prices in cents)
# @name lot
POST http://localhost:3000/lots
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sellerId": "{{seller.response.body.id}}", "title": "Токарный станок", "price": 25000000, "stock": 1, "deliveryMethods": ["pickup", "freight"] }

###
PATCH http://localhost:3000/lots/{{lot.response.body.id}}/publication
Content-Type: application/json

{ "published": true }

### Catalog: published lots, newest first; q searches the title and the seller's name or email.
# Next page: ?after=<nextAfter from the previous response>
GET http://localhost:3000/lots?q=станок&limit=20

### Price change (new price and a history row, in one transaction)
PATCH http://localhost:3000/lots/{{lot.response.body.id}}/price
Content-Type: application/json

{ "price": 26000000 }

### Stock change: a delta, not a total (negative below zero -> 409)
PATCH http://localhost:3000/lots/{{lot.response.body.id}}/stock
Content-Type: application/json

{ "delta": 2 }

### Purchase (FOR UPDATE on the lot and both wallets). Out of stock / no funds -> 409
POST http://localhost:3000/deals
Content-Type: application/json

{ "buyerId": "{{buyer.response.body.id}}", "lotId": "{{lot.response.body.id}}", "quantity": 1 }

### Lot card. Every view is an event in Kafka (topic lot-views, key = visitor IP).
# X-Forwarded-For sets the visitor IP when TRUST_PROXY is on (the Compose stack). 300+ views
# a minute from one IP get it banned: this request then answers 429.
GET http://localhost:3000/lots/{{lot.response.body.id}}
X-Forwarded-For: 203.0.113.7
